# fisher-82i, 2026-11-26. Staged for fisher-b0b.
# Token separators observed in Stockfish 19 (sf_19, edb0d9d), Homebrew arm64 bottle:
# UCIEngine::loop reads the command token with operator>> under the C locale.
# https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish/blob/edb0d9db6731067ec50ce619ff372b463bc4dd5d/src/uci.cpp#L94-L113
# See README.md for the probe input, its output and a hex dump of each send that holds a special byte.
# Send the bytes 69 73 72 65 61 64 79 09 69 73 72 65 61 64 79 0A: horizontal tab
# separates tokens inside one command, so this is isready with the argument
# isready. Stockfish answers one readyok. An engine that ended the command at
# the horizontal tab would read two commands and answer two.
> isready\tisready
# UCI isready/readyok.
< readyok
# UCI quit. A second readyok would arrive before exit and fail here.
> quit
! exit
